  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The Trajectory Refinement for Emission Modeling (TRIM) framework post-processes microsimulated vehicle trajectories using mixed-integer quadratic programming to eliminate nonphysical acceleration and jerk fluctuations. Validated against high-resolution UAV-derived ground truth across three car-following models (Wiedemann 99, Krauss, and the Intelligent Driver Model), the optimization framework reduces total emission estimation errors to within 9% for nitrogen oxides and 7% for PM 2.5.",
      "why": "It provides a platform-independent, standardized method to correct systematic overestimation of vehicular emissions in traffic microsimulations without requiring modification of the underlying simulation engines."
